exit: 0
--- stdout
Description:
  Generate a new valid API key

Usage:
  api-key:generate [options]

Options:
  -m, --name=NAME                        The unique name by which this API key will be known
  -e, --expiration-date=EXPIRATION-DATE  The date in which the API key should expire. Use any valid PHP format
  -a, --author-only                      Adds the "AUTHORED_SHORT_URLS" role to the new API key
  -d, --domain-only=DOMAIN-ONLY          Adds the "DOMAIN_SPECIFIC" role to the new API key, with provided domain
  -o, --no-orphan-visits                 Adds the "NO_ORPHAN_VISITS" role to the new API key
  -h, --help                             Display help for the given command. When no command is given display help for the list command
      --silent                           Do not output any message
  -q, --quiet                            Only errors are displayed. All other output is suppressed
  -V, --version                          Display this application version
      --ansi|--no-ansi                   Force (or disable --no-ansi) ANSI output
  -n, --no-interaction                   Do not ask any interactive question
  -v|vv|vvv, --verbose                   Increase the verbosity of messages: 1 for normal output, 2 for more verbose output and 3 for debug

Help:
  The api-key:generate generates a new valid API key.
  
      /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:generate
  
  You can optionally set its name for tracking purposes with --name or -m:
  
      /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:generate --name Alice
  
  You can optionally set its expiration date with --expiration-date or -e:
  
      /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:generate --expiration-date 2020-01-01
--- stderr
